A||||6||CanadianGT||Forum member breaks down in front of my house!||||1||
Z||000000||CanadianGT||08-15-2001||11:18 AM||||Hi,<BR>while installing a cd player in my car yesterday, this awesome looking 84 pulls over in front of my house and it just dies!  I went up to the guy ( Jerricko) and asked him what happened.  He said his car stalled out.  I told him about this forum and he is a member!  Anyhow, we tried to get it running last night, but to no avail.  This is what happened.  Yesterday, he went and got a new 2 1/8 inch from the muffler back put on.  As he was driving home it started putting out smoke like crazy.  so much, it would come in threw the sunroof. In addition his car was loosing power like crazy.  It had nothing. Whenever he tried to turn it back on  , it would run for a few second then stall.  He said he has jsut changed one spark plug that day, but none of the others.  So i changed 2 more for him, but the other one is stuck in there.  They were all gapped dfferently too.  I regaped all the ones we could get out to .060.  I then checked the oil.  He had litterally only about a 3/4 0f a litre in there, and it was like sludge.  He said he had not changed it since last summer.  I changed it right away.  When we tried to fire the car back up, it would not run.  It would just turn over.  Then smoke started to come from where the air filter is!!  I took off the cover and saw it would shoot gas while trying to turn over, but it would never catch.  then when He stopped trying to turn it over, a huge pile of smoke would come up through the air intake, and also was comming up from where the oil dipstick is!!!  There was also a sand like substance in his intake there.  I left it for the night, and when I came out this morning it would start then die.  Finally I kept my foot on the gas for about 30 seconds and let go..it stayed even at about 1300 rpm for about 3 minutes.  Then when I put it in gear ( automatic)  the engine would really start to shutter and die out immediatly.  I also I think i hear a slight knock sound when giving it gas, but cant tell if its the new exaust hitting the frame. If there is a knock, you can hardly hear it at all. Sorry for the really long post but I wanted to give you all the information so you could give me the best advice possible.  Thanks sooooo  much.<BR>PeAcE<BR>Kyle||||reg||1
Z||000001||Formula88||08-15-2001||12:32 PM||||The smoke coming up through the dipstick and PCV tube make me think it has a broken piston ring.  If he just got a new exhaust, was he driving it hard to check it out?  It could have over-revved and cracked a piston ring.  Check the compression and go from there.||||reg||13
Z||000002||stsmithgt||08-15-2001||01:16 PM||||The oil in an 84' not changed since last summer?  3/4 of a liter of oil?  When was the oil level checked last.  That white smoke must of smell like neglect.  Enough things go wrong with these old cars even with constant attention.  Worrying about exhaust tips before more important maintanence?  Somebody's got their priority list all cluster phuked.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/apeshakinghead.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by stsmithgt (edited 08-15-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||California Kid||08-15-2001||01:33 PM||||[QUOTE]Originally posted by stsmithgt:<BR>[B]Somebody's got their priority list all cluster phuked.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/apeshakinghead.gif"> <P>Just loved your response and the monkey !!!  Certainly sounds like the engine is trying to tell him something, in it's last fatal breaths.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||scott_g||08-15-2001||01:38 PM||||Hey guys, <P>Not a fiero owner yet, but currently looking into it.  Not sure about the smoke, but have you checked the fuel pressure/condition of the lines?  I had an old montecarlo that had the same symptoms (stalling, not wanting to start, etc.).  The fuel line was rusted through in one spot and had a small pinhole in it.  Although it was getting gas to the carb, it was also sucking air through the pinhole.  A couple new lines and it was patched up for another term as the winter beater.  Good luck<P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||EdsB52||08-15-2001||02:00 PM||||Is Jerricko related to Maniak84?||||reg||1
Z||000006||stsmithgt||08-15-2001||03:10 PM||||I couldn't help smirking putting that monkey up there. Hah!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><BR>I keep a close watch over my car and it still can end up in the shop.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/clipart_horror_064.gif">  Sometimes I go crazy trying to catch the problem before raises it's ugly head.  Preventative maintanence is supposed to keep the car from needing a shop.  There's NO room for negligence or ignorance, but there is room for bad spelling. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  Oh well.  The MONEY PIT should be mechanically sound $$$$.$$now...$$$.$$.. now..$$$$.$$.. now?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>------------------<BR>My work of art.(in progress.)    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/carpicsig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
